#====================================================================
# DRAFT - OHOS conan aggregated env only propagates whitelisted vars;
#   recipe env.define for other vars is silently dropped
# 触发事件: gtk2 2.24.33 真机适配(2026-09-13)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-conan-aggregated-env-whitelist
trigger_tool:           conan|autoconf|config.status
phase:                  building|configuration
error_signature: >-
  working directory cannot be determined|
  getcwd: cannot access parent directories|
  ac_tmp=$tmp

severity:               1
category:               conan|ohos|environment|autotools|portability
match_keywords:         env.define, whitelist, TMPDIR, PWD, PKG_CONFIG,
                        conanbuildenv, aggregated env, job env.sh,
                        env.sh inheritance, 静默丢失
title:                   OHOS conan aggregated env propagates only whitelisted variables; recipe env.define for other variables is silently dropped

root_cause: >-
  The OHOS-adapted conan writes its aggregated env file (conanbuildenv-*.sh)
  for a whitelist of variables only (PATH, PKG_CONFIG_PATH, CONFIG_SHELL,
  SHELL, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, AUTOTOOLS_DEV_*). A recipe env.define for TMPDIR,
  PWD, or PKG_CONFIG never reaches later build stages through this file,
  although a subset of effects arrives via direct os.environ mutation of the
  conan process — producing inconsistent "works sometimes" behavior. Autoconf
  tools that validate or fall back on these variables then fail: mksh validates
  $PWD and falls back to a getcwd that returns EBADF on the distributed fs.
affected_scope: >-
  Every OHOS conan recipe that sets non-whitelisted environment variables for
  configure/make steps. Observed losses: TMPDIR (clang temp files land on the
  read-only /tmp), PWD (mksh getcwd validation fails), PKG_CONFIG (config.status
  probes degrade).
verification_cmd: >-
  cd <build folder> && . conan/conanbuild.sh && for v in TMPDIR PWD PKG_CONFIG; do printf "%s=[%s]\n" "$v" "$(printenv $v)"; done

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           job-env-inheritance
rec_description: >
  Export the needed variables in the job-level env.sh (sourced before conan
  create) so the conan process inherits them and every child — including
  libtool scripts, config.status, and compile tools — sees them through
  normal inheritance. Diagnose by sourcing the aggregated env file and
  echoing each expected variable; empty brackets confirm a dropped variable.
  For path-like needs that cannot be expressed as environment variables,
  rewrite the consuming build script in the recipe (sed the generated
  file) instead of relying on env propagation.
rec_command:            echo "export TMPDIR=/storage/Users/currentUser/<job>/tmp" >> <job>/env.sh && conan create ...
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               job-env-sh-inheritance

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      recipe-intrinsic-rewrite
fallback_description: >
  When a variable cannot be injected via inheritance (e.g. per-package
  isolation is required), rewrite the consuming build script directly in
  the recipe (sed the generated configure/config.status) to use an
  intrinsic path instead of the environment variable.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          recipe-sed-intrinsic

forbid_1_pattern:       env\.define\((TMPDIR|PWD|PKG_CONFIG)\).*claims.*fixed
forbid_1_reason:        Declaring the fix without verifying the variable actually propagates through the aggregated env leaves the failure in place.
forbid_1_consequence:   The same build failure recurs on the next device run.

principles:             P016
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-conan-aggregated-env-whitelist.md
last_updated:           2026-09-13
source_event: >-
  gtk2 2.24.33 device build: TMPDIR/PWD/PKG_CONFIG env.define values absent
  from the aggregated conanbuildenv file

authors:                codex
